# Entry 12: Simplified implementation (coding task)
entries.append({
    "id": str(int(time.time() * 1000)),
    "level": "L3",
    "interface": "gesvdj",
    "instruction": "Write a simplified GESVDJ implementation outline for the tall case (m >= n). Include the main algorithmic steps with proper BLAS/LAPACK calls.",
    "context_text": "Implement a basic GESVDJ for tall matrices showing the key steps: gramian formation, eigensolve, and QR extraction.",
    "code_blocks": [],
    "answer": "Simplified GESVDJ implementation (tall case m >= n):\n\n```cpp\n// File: gesvdj_simple.hpp\n#pragma once\n\n#include \"rocblas.hpp\"\n#include \"roclapack_syevj_heevj.hpp\"\n#include \"roclapack_geqrf.hpp\"\n#include \"rocauxiliary_orgqr_ungqr.hpp\"\n\ntemplate <typename T, typename S>\nrocblas_status gesvdj_simple_tall(\n    rocblas_handle handle,\n    const rocblas_svect left_svect,\n    const rocblas_svect right_svect,\n    const rocblas_int m,  // m >= n\n    const rocblas_int n,\n    T* A,  // m x n (destroyed)\n    const rocblas_int lda,\n    const S abstol,\n    S* residual,\n    const rocblas_int max_sweeps,\n    rocblas_int* n_sweeps,\n    S* S_out,  // Singular values\n    T* U,      // m x n or m x m\n    const rocblas_int ldu,\n    T* V,      // n x n\n    const rocblas_int ldv,\n    rocblas_int* info)\n{\n    // Allocate workspace\n    T* V_work;  // n x n for eigenvectors\n    T* U_work;  // m x n for A*V\n    T* tau;     // n Householder scalars\n    // ... (allocate SYEVJ workspace)\n    \n    hipMalloc(&V_work, n*n*sizeof(T));\n    hipMalloc(&U_work, m*n*sizeof(T));\n    hipMalloc(&tau, n*sizeof(T));\n    \n    hipStream_t stream;\n    rocblas_get_stream(handle, &stream);\n    \n    // Constants\n    T one = T(1.0);\n    T minone = T(-1.0);\n    T zero = T(0.0);\n    \n    // Step 1: Form -A^T*A (n x n)\n    // V_work = -A^T * A\n    rocblas_gemm(handle,\n                 rocblas_operation_conjugate_transpose,\n                 rocblas_operation_none,\n                 n, n, m,\n                 &minone,        // alpha = -1\n                 A, lda,         // A^T\n                 A, lda,         // A\n                 &zero,          // beta = 0\n                 V_work, n);     // Result: -A^T*A\n    \n    // Step 2: Eigendecompose -A^T*A = V * Lambda * V^T\n    // V_work input: -A^T*A\n    // V_work output: Eigenvectors (right singular vectors)\n    // S_out output: Eigenvalues (will become singular values)\n    rocsolver_syevj_heevj_template<false, false, T>(\n        handle,\n        rocblas_esort_ascending,     // Ascending eigenvalues\n        rocblas_evect_original,      // Compute eigenvectors\n        rocblas_fill_upper,          // Use upper triangle\n        n,                           // Size\n        V_work, 0, n, 0,             // In/Out: -A^T*A -> V\n        abstol,                      // Tolerance\n        residual,                    // Residual output\n        max_sweeps,                  // Max iterations\n        n_sweeps,                    // Actual iterations\n        S_out, 0,                    // Eigenvalues output\n        info, 1,                     // Info, batch=1\n        /* workspace pointers */);\n    \n    // Step 3: Compute A*V (m x n)\n    // U_work = A * V_work\n    rocblas_gemm(handle,\n                 rocblas_operation_none,\n                 rocblas_operation_none,\n                 m, n, n,\n                 &one,           // alpha = 1\n                 A, lda,         // A\n                 V_work, n,      // V\n                 &zero,          // beta = 0\n                 U_work, m);     // Result: A*V\n    \n    // Step 4: QR factorization of A*V\n    // U_work = Q * R where R diagonal = singular values\n    rocsolver_geqrf_template<false, false, T>(\n        handle,\n        m, n,\n        U_work, 0, m, 0,  // In/Out: A*V -> Q (implicit)\n        tau, n,           // Householder scalars\n        1,                // Batch count\n        /* workspace */);\n    \n    // Step 5: Extract singular values and fix signs\n    // Launch kernel to:\n    //   - S_out[i] = |U_work[i,i]|  (R diagonal)\n    //   - If U_work[i,i] < 0: negate V_work[:,i]\n    rocblas_int blocks = (n-1)/32 + 1;\n    ROCSOLVER_LAUNCH_KERNEL(\n        (gesvdj_finalize<T,S>),\n        dim3(blocks, 1, 1), dim3(32, 1, 1),\n        0, stream,\n        n, S_out, 0,\n        U_work, m, 0,\n        V_work, n, 0);\n    \n    // Step 6: Generate U from Q (if requested)\n    if(left_svect != rocblas_svect_none)\n    {\n        rocblas_int ncol = (left_svect == rocblas_svect_all) ? m : n;\n        \n        // U = orgqr(U_work, tau)\n        rocsolver_orgqr_ungqr_template<false, false, T>(\n            handle,\n            m, ncol, n,\n            U_work, 0, m, 0,\n            tau, n,\n            1,  // Batch\n            /* workspace */);\n        \n        // Copy to U output\n        // U_work (m x ncol) -> U\n        copy_matrix(U_work, m, U, ldu, m, ncol);\n    }\n    \n    // Step 7: Transpose V to V^T (if requested)\n    if(right_svect != rocblas_svect_none)\n    {\n        // V_work (n x n) -> V (transpose)\n        ROCSOLVER_LAUNCH_KERNEL(\n            (copy_trans_mat<T>),\n            dim3((n-1)/32+1, (n-1)/32+1, 1),\n            dim3(32, 32, 1),\n            0, stream,\n            rocblas_operation_conjugate_transpose,\n            n, n,\n            V_work, 0, n, 0,\n            V, 0, ldv, 0);\n    }\n    \n    // Cleanup\n    hipFree(V_work);\n    hipFree(U_work);\n    hipFree(tau);\n    \n    return rocblas_status_success;\n}\n```\n\nKey algorithmic steps:\n\n1. Gramian formation: -A^T*A\n   - GEMM with alpha=-1\n   - Result: n x n symmetric\n   - Stored in V workspace\n\n2. Eigendecomposition: SYEVJ\n   - Input: -A^T*A (destroyed)\n   - Output: V (eigenvectors), Lambda (eigenvalues)\n   - Lambda -> S (will be squared to get singular values)\n\n3. Matrix multiply: A*V\n   - GEMM: m x n result\n   - Stored in U workspace\n\n4. QR factorization: GEQRF\n   - Input: A*V (destroyed)\n   - Output: Q (Householder), R (upper triangular)\n   - R diagonal contains singular values\n\n5. Sign correction: gesvdj_finalize\n   - Extract |R[i,i]| -> S[i]\n   - Negate V[:,i] if R[i,i] < 0\n\n6. Generate U: ORGQR\n   - Expand Householder reflectors\n   - Q -> U (orthogonal matrix)\n\n7. Transpose V: Copy kernel\n   - V -> V^T (conjugate transpose)\n\nUsage:\n```cpp\nfloat A[12] = {...};  // 4x3 matrix\nfloat S[3];           // Singular values\nfloat U[12];          // 4x3 left vectors\nfloat V[9];           // 3x3 right vectors\nfloat residual;\nrocblas_int n_sweeps, info;\n\ngesvdj_simple_tall<float>(\n    handle,\n    rocblas_svect_singular,\n    rocblas_svect_all,\n    4, 3, A, 4,\n    1e-6f, &residual, 30, &n_sweeps,\n    S, U, 4, V, 3, &info);\n```",
    "rationale": "Simplified GESVDJ for tall matrices: (1) Form -A^T*A via GEMM, (2) Eigendecompose with SYEVJ to get V and eigenvalues, (3) Compute A*V via GEMM, (4) QR factorization with GEQRF to get U and singular values on R diagonal, (5) Extract/fix signs with gesvdj_finalize, (6) Generate U with ORGQR, (7) Transpose V. This demonstrates the core Jacobi SVD algorithm.",
    "tags": ["coding", "gesvdj", "implementation", "svd", "jacobi", "algorithm"]
})
